If `showTags` turns off before scanning finishes, `hasFetchedTagCandidatesRef` blocks every later scan. The canceled promise cannot update `tagCandidateState`, so tagged results remain unavailable until the modal reopens.

<details>
<summary>Learn more</summary>

The ref records that a request started, not that usable candidates were stored. Effect cleanup cancels the state update but never clears the ref. Turning the toggle off during the vault scan therefore leaves `tagCandidateState` loading and prevents a replacement request. React Strict Mode also performs a development-only setup-cleanup-setup cycle, which reaches the same state without user interaction.

