**Race condition: stale tag candidates when nodeTypes config changes**

The `hasFetchedTagCandidatesRef` prevents refetching when `plugin.settings.nodeTypes` changes after a successful fetch. If the user modifies the node types configuration (adds/removes/changes tags), the cached tag candidates remain stale and will never update.

**What breaks:** Tag search results won't reflect the current configuration until the modal is completely remounted.

**Fix:** Reset the ref when nodeTypes changes:
```typescript
const prevNodeTypesRef = useRef(plugin.settings.nodeTypes);
useEffect(() => {
  if (prevNodeTypesRef.current !== plugin.settings.nodeTypes) {
    hasFetchedTagCandidatesRef.current = false;
    prevNodeTypesRef.current = plugin.settings.nodeTypes;
  }
}, [plugin.settings.nodeTypes]);
```

Or include the ref reset in the fetch effect's cleanup when nodeTypes change specifically.
```suggestion

